                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>-United States</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'> stands out with a massive GDP and low relative debt-to-GDP.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>-Japan and Germany</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'> also show strong GDP with manageable debt levels.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>-Some countries like </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>Iceland</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'> show small GDP and </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>high debt</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'> — riskier investment zones.</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>-Large GDP economies with low/moderate debt are </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'>safe bets</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='18'> for real estate development due to their economic stability and liquidity.</run>
